    "w": 816,
    "h": 1056,
    "html": "<div style=\"width: 816px; height: 1056px; box-sizing: border-box; background: #FFFEFB; color: #1B2440; font-family: 'Public Sans', sans-serif; display: flex; flex-direction: column\">\n<header style=\"background: #16306E; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 40px 56px 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; border-bottom: 8px solid #C8231E\">\n<p style=\"margin: 0; font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 3px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #F2A7A3\">Referring provider guide</p>\n<h1 style=\"margin: 0; font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 38px; line-height: 1.1\">Joint Pain Program</h1>\n</header>\n<main style=\"flex: 1; min-height: 0; padding: 30px 56px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 19.8px\">\n\n<p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 19.8px; line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 600; color: #16306E\">Image-guided embolization reduces abnormal blood flow to inflamed synovium and tendon tissue. It is a next step for patients stuck between conservative care and surgery.</p>\n<div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr; gap: 30.8px; align-items: start\"><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 11.0px; min-width: 0\"><h2 style=\"margin: 0; font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 23.1px; line-height: 1.2; color: #16306E\">Who to Refer</h2><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 7.7px\"><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 9.9px; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 15.4px; line-height: 1.4\"><span style=\"flex: none; width: 16px; color: #C8231E; font-weight: 800\">✓</span><span>Joint or tendon pain for 3+ months despite PT, NSAIDs and injections</span></div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 9.9px; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 15.4px; line-height: 1.4\"><span style=\"flex: none; width: 16px; color: #C8231E; font-weight: 800\">✓</span><span>Not ready for, not eligible for, or wanting to delay surgery</span></div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 9.9px; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 15.4px; line-height: 1.4\"><span style=\"flex: none; width: 16px; color: #C8231E; font-weight: 800\">✓</span><span><b>Knee (GAE):</b> mild to moderate OA (KL 1–3), or pain after replacement</span></div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 9.9px; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 15.4px; line-height: 1.4\"><span style=\"flex: none; width: 16px; color: #C8231E; font-weight: 800\">✓</span><span><b>Shoulder, hip, hand (TAME):</b> adhesive capsulitis, tendinopathy, OA</span></div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 9.9px; align-items: flex-start; font-size: 15.4px; line-height: 1.4\"><span style=\"flex: none; width: 16px; color: #C8231E; font-weight: 800\">✓</span><span><b>Heel (PFE):</b> plantar fasciitis despite standard care</span></div></div></div><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.0px; min-width: 0\"><figure style=\"margin: 0; background: #FFFFFF; border: 1px solid #E2DED4; border-radius: 14px; padding: 12px 12px 10px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6.6px\"><img src=\"assets/healthy-vs-painful-joint.jpg\" alt=\"Two joints side by side: a healthy joint and a painful, inflamed joint with extra small blood vessels\" style=\"width: 100%; height: 200px; object-fit: contain; object-position: 50% 50%; display: block\"><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14.3px; line-height: 1.4; color: #4A5568; text-align: center\">Inflamed synovium grows new small vessels; embolization targets them.</p></figure></div></div>\n<div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 13.2px\"><div style=\"background: #F7F6F2; border-top: 4px solid #16306E; border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px 14px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 5.5px\"><p style=\"margin: 0; font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 15.95px; color: #16306E\">What the evidence shows</p><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14.85px; line-height: 1.42\">Knee GAE is the most studied. Open-label studies report meaningful pain improvement, and the SIR issued a supportive position statement in 2026.<sup style=\"font-size: 9.35px\">1</sup> Small sham-controlled trials are mixed, and larger trials are under way.<sup style=\"font-size: 9.35px\">2</sup> Evidence for other joints is early.<sup style=\"font-size: 9.35px\">3</sup> Embolic agents are used off-label for joint pain; results vary.</p></div><div style=\"background: #F7F6F2; border-top: 4px solid #C8231E; border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px 14px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 5.5px\"><p style=\"margin: 0; font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 15.95px; color: #16306E\">Coverage</p><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14.85px; line-height: 1.42\">There is no GAE-specific CPT code, and many commercial payers consider joint embolization investigational. We verify benefits and obtain prior authorization before any procedure.</p></div></div>\n<div style=\"display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 13.2px\"><div style=\"background: #F7F6F2; border-top: 4px solid #16306E; border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px 14px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 5.5px\"><p style=\"margin: 0; font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 15.95px; color: #16306E\">Outpatient</p><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14.3px; line-height: 1.42\">Small groin or wrist puncture; home the same day</p></div><div style=\"background: #F7F6F2; border-top: 4px solid #16306E; border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px 14px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 5.5px\"><p style=\"margin: 0; font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 15.95px; color: #16306E\">No incision</p><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14.3px; line-height: 1.42\">Small puncture; no stitches</p></div><div style=\"background: #F7F6F2; border-top: 4px solid #16306E; border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px 14px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 5.5px\"><p style=\"margin: 0; font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 15.95px; color: #16306E\">Follow-up</p><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 14.3px; line-height: 1.42\">Outcomes shared at 1 and 3 months</p></div></div>\n<div style=\"flex: 1\"></div>\n<p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 10.45px; line-height: 1.4; color: #6B7280\">1. SIR position statement on genicular artery embolization. J Vasc Interv Radiol 2026. 2. Milhem F et al. J Orthop 2025 (systematic review of sham-controlled GAE trials). 3. Hindsø L et al. Cardiovasc Intervent Radiol 2021;44:1699-1708.</p>\n\n</main>\n<footer style=\"padding: 14px 56px 26px; display: flex; justify-content: flex-start; gap: 14px; font-size: 12px; color: #4A5568\">\n<span style=\"font-weight: 700; color: #16306E\">4</span><span>Advanced Joint Pain &amp; Vascular Center · Heart Vascular &amp; Leg Center</span>\n</footer>\n</div>"
