    "html": "<div style=\"width: 1056px; height: 816px; box-sizing: border-box; background: #FFFEFB; color: #1B2440; font-family: 'Public Sans', sans-serif; display: flex; flex-direction: column; padding: 34px 44px 26px; gap: 20px\">\n<div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-end; gap: 24px; border-bottom: 5px solid #C8231E; padding-bottom: 14px\">\n<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px\"><p style=\"margin: 0; font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif; font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px; letter-spacing: 3px; text-transform: uppercase; color: #C8231E\">Joint pain</p>\n<h1 style=\"margin: 0; font-family: 'Montserrat', sans-serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 44px; line-height: 1.05; color: #16306E\">Healthy Joint vs. Painful Joint</h1></div>\n<div style=\"display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px\"><img src=\"assets/logo-hvlc.png\" alt=\"Heart Vascular &amp; Leg Center logo\" style=\"height: 34px; width: 78px; object-fit: contain; object-position: left center\"><span style=\"width: 1px; height: 27px; background: #E2DED4\"></span><img src=\"assets/logo-long-nodivision.png\" alt=\"Advanced Joint Pain &amp; Vascular Center logo\" style=\"height: 34px; width: 129px; object-fit: contain; object-position: left center\"></div></div>\n<main style=\"flex: 1; min-height: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px\"><div style=\"flex: 1; min-height: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px\"><div style=\"flex: 1; min-height: 0; min-width: 0; background: #FFFFFF; border-radius: 18px; overflow: hidden; display: flex\"><img src=\"assets/healthy-vs-painful-joint.jpg\" alt=\"A healthy joint with smooth cartilage beside a painful joint with worn cartilage and a swollen, red lining\" style=\"width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 50% 45%; display: block\"></div></div><div style=\"display: flex; gap: 24px\"><div style=\"flex: 1; min-width: 0; display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; border-top: 4px solid #C8231E; padding-top: 12px\"><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.32; color: #1B2440\">Healthy: smooth cartilage and a thin lining</p></div><div style=\"flex: 1; min-width: 0; display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; border-top: 4px solid #C8231E; padding-top: 12px\"><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.32; color: #1B2440\">Painful: worn cartilage and a swollen, inflamed lining</p></div><div style=\"flex: 1; min-width: 0; display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; border-top: 4px solid #C8231E; padding-top: 12px\"><p style=\"margin: 0; font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.32; color: #1B2440\">Inflammation, not just wear, causes much of the pain</p></div></div></main></div>"
